---
description: Prefer the Review herd and report over raw grep when a graph is present
alwaysApply: true
---

When a Graphide Review graph is present, read the herd and the report before grepping the tree.

A graph is present when `extension/scripts/live-snap.json` exists, a `graphide review --root <folder> --json` snapshot is on hand, or the Review desk herd (`#herd`) is open.

Read `programs`, `flows`, `findings`, `coverage`, and `bubbles` from that snapshot. Grep only a span the report already names.

Agents never stamp. Do not write `.graphide/stamps/` and do not run `graphide stamp`.

To start a cut and wait: `node scripts/agent-herd.mjs --root <folder> --wait`. Exit 0 means the focused cut is blocked. Exit 2 means the review settled and that cut is not blocked.

Map stays community LOD. This is not a terminal and not a worktree list.
